  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pan Amazon Ecclesial Network REPAM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to assist in the defence of human rights and the enforceability of rights in the Pan-Amazonian region.

Focusing on the different areas of the Church in the nine countries of the region with territory in the Amazon basin, REPAM, the Ecclesial Network of the pan-Amazon Region, was set up officially in September 2014 bringing together a range of pastoral experience of the laity, hierarchy, religious congregations, and the major coordinating bodies of the Church in the region. Its overall aim is to encourage the transformation of the reality of the Amazon region based on the Gospel, &quot;taking care of creation and building a just and fraternal society, promoting the integral and sustainable human development and the perspective of the good life, so that people have life and have it abundantly&#x201d;.

The project provides support for the process of consolidation of the REPAM network and its international advocacy in the field of human rights, and for the development of its methodological approach to the training of agents for the promotion and defence of human rights and the enforceability of rights in Pan-Amazonia.</narrative>
  </description>
